<<if $MichaelSocial > 50>>
    Michael Reyes is your friend and classmate. He has a reputation as a bully, and to be fair he is one, but you’ve been able to break past that to see the well-meaning, if not occasionally dickish, boy underneath. He has a small group of friends at his side at most times, though he seems to enjoy your company more, whether it is due to your personality or ability to occasionally keep up with him, you’re not sure. <br>
    <br>
<<elseif $MichaelSocial > -10>>
    Michael Reyes is your classmate and the local bully of Preston. He has a reputation for picking on anyone smaller or weaker than him, or just anyone he finds annoying honestly, and constantly getting detention. Often flanked by a small group of goons at his beck and call, he uses them to intimidate and get his way with anyone he can’t handle on his own. <br>
    <br>
<<else>>
    Michael Reyes, Preston’s local asshole bully, is a constant thorn in your side. You’ve often found yourself on the opposing side of his smug face and annoying voice. He likes to pick on and bully people he can’t control, constantly keeping a small group of goons at his side for anyone he’s too afraid to handle on his own. He is generally an overall jerk. <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

<<if $CompletedQuests.includes("Michael: Little Bear")>>
    A coincidence led to you helping Michael’s grandmother move some boxes around, which caught the normally cool and collected Michael off-guard. Despite his tough appearance, it seems Michael does have a kinder side when it comes to his grandmother, just don’t tell anyone that unless you want to get punched in the face. <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

